# =============================================================================
# E3-DoH Reproducibility — Dataset SHA-256 Manifest
# =============================================================================
#
# This file records the SHA-256 of every external dataset used by
# Chapter 5. It is checked by data/download_datasets.py when
# --verify-sha256 is passed (the default in full mode).
#
# The entries below are `<TO_BE_POPULATED>` until the first successful
# full-mode download. To populate:
#
#     python data/download_datasets.py --mode full --verify-sha256
#
# That run will compute and log the observed hash for each dataset
# to outputs/logs/dataset_hashes.json. Paste those hashes into the
# lines below, then commit this file in the same commit as the
# dataset download log.
#
# Format (standard sha256sum):
#     <64-hex-digest>  <dataset-id>
#
# Until populated, download_datasets.py issues a warning but proceeds
# (strict mode with --strict-hash turns the warning into a hard
# failure). This is documented in the script's module docstring.
#
# =============================================================================

# DS-1: Zenodo encrypted-DNS corpus (32 GB)
# DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.5957677
<TO_BE_POPULATED>  DS-1

# DS-2: DoH Real-World 2022 corpus (4 GB)
# DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.5957677
<TO_BE_POPULATED>  DS-2

# DS-3: Kosekmi 2022 PAM DNS-over-QUIC collection (3 GB)
# DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.5957677
<TO_BE_POPULATED>  DS-3
